Spec: Signature-pinned Binder client

Purpose:
  Offer asynchronous control calls with verified binding and explicit close.

Owns:
  ./BrokerClient.java

References:
  ./PeerPin.sdd
  ./ClientRuntime.sdd
  /contracts/java/src/main/java/dev/linkgate/contracts/ControlReply.sdd
  ./ControlSession.sdd

Must:
  Verify service metadata and current signing certificates before binding, after callback and around every hello call.
  Use an explicit component and action, validate the AIDL descriptor and listen for Binder death and binding loss.
  Complete bind and control futures after a two-second timeout without claiming native Binder interruption.
  Keep one active request per client and never automatically rebind, retry or enable experimental capabilities.
  On failure, cancellation or close, discard late results and unbind each accepted binding once, including late bind completion.
  Retain the runtime lease until binding cleanup finishes; release failed binds without leaking leases.
  Recheck the same installed peer around descriptor attachment and close descriptors from failed or late calls.

  Expose explicit relay opening without embedding a backend runtime or changing the direct method into implicit fallback.
  Expose formal open/status/attach/close and appended stream-reference Binder attachment through the same pinned session; require explicit experimental opt-in and discard late descriptors.
